  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Natural sweeteners, e.g., sucrose add to calorie intake and therefore many people prefer to use artificial sweeteners. Ortho-sulphobenzimide, also called saccharin, is the first popular artificial sweetening agent. It is about 550 times as sweet as cane sugar. Aspartame is 100 times as sweet as cane sugar.&nbsp;Sucralose is 600 times as sweet as cane sugar.&nbsp;Alitame is an artificial sweetener that has 1000 times the sweetness value of cane sugar.&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
